  m_Name: FishTutorialContent
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  Role: 0
  RoleLabel: Fish
  Title: How to survive the hotel
  Summary: '{input:Game/Move} Walk. {input:Game/Run} Run. {input:Game/Jump} Jump.
    {input:<Pointer>/position} Aim the spotlight. Hold run when jumping to clear
    the dining cart. Dining cart hits knock back and stun without draining health.
    Avoid the angler''s lethal horizontal path and the swinging/falling chandelier;
    reach the stairwell and use {input:Game/Interact} to challenge the ghost. Damaging
    traps drain health; dead fish spectate. Dining cart hits do not drain health.
    Fish wins at 3 goals; ghost at 1. Others spectate. Choose Ready, wait for everyone,
    then the 10-second ghost setup before moving. Hallway return includes another
    ghost head start.'
  Instructions:
  - Heading: Move and jump
    Body: '{input:Game/Move} Walk. {input:Game/Run} Run. {input:Game/Jump} Jump from
      the ground.'
  - Heading: See and avoid traps
    Body: '{input:<Pointer>/position} Aim the spotlight. Hold run when launching
      a jump to clear the dining cart. Watch for the angler''s lethal horizontal
      rush and the swinging chandelier above.'
  - Heading: Health and spectating
    Body: Damaging traps drain health. Dead fish spectate as their soul rises away.
      Dining cart hits only knock back and stun; the piranha effect clears on recovery.
  - Heading: Stairwell challenge
    Body: Reach the stairwell door and use {input:Game/Interact}. {input:<Mouse>/leftButton}
      Hold and drag your striker across both axes of your own half to hit the cue
      ball. Drag sideline defenses onto your half; they bounce the ball and break
      after 1-3 hits.
  - Heading: Win and return
    Body: Fish wins at 3 goals; ghost wins at 1. Other participants spectate. The
      hallway return includes another ghost head start.
  - Heading: Round start
    Body: Read the role page and deliberately choose Ready. Everyone must be ready;
      wait through the 10-second ghost setup before moving.
